From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:09:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/panel: jadard-jd9365da-h3: probe asynchronously

Attaching the second panel binds the whole Rockchip display pipeline, and
the first modeset then prepares and initialises both panels, each ~0.4 s
of sleeps in its power-on sequence (reset 5 + 10 + 130 ms, sleep-out
120 ms, display on 20 ms). With the driver built in, all of that ran
inside jadard_driver_init(), and every initcall after it, the root
file system's included, waited: 0.81 s of a 2.03 s kernel start on the
RG DS+ (initcall_debug).

With PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS the probe runs beside the other
initcalls. The root mount still waits for it through
wait_for_device_probe(), but it now ends at about the time the root SD
card is ready.

Upstream status: candidate. Nothing in the driver depends on probe order.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
index b100b0482..e597a0c18 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
@@ -3454,6 +3454,13 @@ static struct mipi_dsi_driver jadard_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "jadard-jd9365da",
 		.of_match_table = jadard_of_match,
+		/*
+		 * Attaching the panel binds the whole display pipeline, and the
+		 * first modeset sleeps ~0.4 s per panel in prepare and init.
+		 * Built in, that holds up every initcall after it (and so the
+		 * root file system); asynchronously it overlaps them.
+		 */
+		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
 };
 module_mipi_dsi_driver(jadard_driver);
